   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possessives",
     "texto": [
      "**Benim** means «my» and **senin** means «your». The noun takes the ending: **benim annem** (my mother), **senin baban** (your father).",
      "**Onun** means «his» or «her»: **onun kardeşi** (his or her brother or sister). In a normal sentence, the possessive pronoun can be left out: **Annem öğretmen** (my mother is a teacher)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Adjectives",
     "texto": [
      "The adjective goes before the noun: **büyük aile** (big family), **küçük çocuk** (small child). Adjectives do not change form for gender or plural.",
      "**Çok** means «very» or «a lot» and goes before the adjective: **çok iyi** (very good)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
